<h3 class="font-headline-sm text-headline-sm text-on-surface font-semibold text-base sm:text-lg">
              What is the fundamental difference between Cashless and Reimbursement claims?
            </h3>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary faq-icon transition-transform">expand_more</span>
</div>
<div class="font-body-md text-body-md text-secondary leading-relaxed faq-answer hidden pt-2">
            The <strong>Cashless</strong> facility lets members simply show their digital membership card (PRUPrime Healthcare) at a partner hospital. Prudential issues the initial and final guarantee directly to the hospital, so members don't need to pay out of pocket upfront. <strong>Reimbursement</strong>, meanwhile, applies when a member chooses treatment at a non-partner hospital; costs are paid first by the member, then the original receipts and medical resume are submitted to us for reimbursement within 7–14 working days.
          </div>
