<h3 class="font-headline-sm text-headline-sm text-on-surface font-semibold text-base sm:text-lg">
              How long is the waiting period for health and critical illness insurance claims?
            </h3>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary faq-icon transition-transform">expand_more</span>
</div>
<div class="font-body-md text-body-md text-secondary leading-relaxed faq-answer hidden pt-2">
            For work accidents or physical emergencies, protection is active <strong>immediately (0 days)</strong> from policy approval. For common illnesses (viral infections, typhoid, dengue), the waiting period is <strong>30 calendar days</strong>. For 18 specific conditions (such as tumors, kidney stones, hernia), a <strong>12-month</strong> waiting period applies. Advanced-stage critical illness benefit policies generally apply a <strong>90-day</strong> waiting period from the issue date.
          </div>
