              What most often causes a claim to be rejected or delayed?
            </h3>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary faq-icon transition-transform">expand_more</span>
</div>
<div class="font-body-md text-body-md text-secondary leading-relaxed faq-answer hidden pt-2">
            The three main reasons for rejection in the insurance industry are: (1) <em>Non-disclosure</em> or past medical history not disclosed at registration, (2) The claim occurs within the waiting period of an active policy, and (3) Incomplete medical record resume from the attending doctor. This is the advantage of being accompanied by an experienced advisor like Denny Indra: every document is reviewed precisely before submission to ensure 100% clause compliance.
